            <div xml:id="d716">

                <pb facs="1020" n="900" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg900"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2591: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-30T14:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30, 1922—2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 1—1:27 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Technical Board resolves that by reason of absolute inefficiency of the Chinese
                    forces guarding Chinese Eastern resulting in destruction of property, harassing
                    and killing employees by bandits, <pb facs="1021" n="901" xml:id="pg901"/> each
                    representative shall so advise his Government and ask immediate steps be taken
                    to provide proper guard. Copy Peking, Tokio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
